nk:talk-industry-keynote-1-mohit-bansal a nk:Talk ;
    rdfs:label "Agentic Challenges (Trustworthy Collaboration, World Discovery, and Long-Horizon Memory) and Industry-Academia Collaborations" ;
    nk:about nk:topic-agents,
        nk:topic-alignment-safety,
        nk:topic-reasoning-math,
        nk:topic-speech-audio ;
    nk:inSession nk:session-25-1600-session-4-orals-posters- ;
    nk:summary "In this talk, I will discuss 3 major pitfalls and challenges of current state-of-the-art AI agents, and present potential solutions for: (1) Teaching agents to be trustworthy and reliable collaborators based on: social/pragmatic multi-agent interactions via speaker-listener confidence calibration, l" ;
    nk:talkType "Industry keynote" ;
    nk:time "2026-10-25 16:30–17:30" ;
    nk:url "https://2026.emnlp.org/program/keynotes/" .

nk:talk-industry-keynote-2-verena-rieser a nk:Talk ;
    rdfs:label "Toward a Science of Constitutional Alignment: Positive Alignment for Value-Based Agents" ;
    nk:about nk:topic-agents,
        nk:topic-alignment-safety,
        nk:topic-evaluation,
        nk:topic-reasoning-math ;
    nk:inSession nk:session-26-900-session-5-orals-posters- ;
    nk:summary "As AI systems become increasingly autonomous, we need a rigorous new science to ensure that more capable models make safe, reliable choices even when we aren’t looking. A promising direction is positive alignment: anchoring models to an intrinsic “north star” of high-level normative values rather th" ;
    nk:talkType "Industry keynote" ;
    nk:time "2026-10-26 9:00–10:30" ;
    nk:url "https://2026.emnlp.org/program/keynotes/" .

nk:talk-keynote-1-pascale-fung a nk:Talk ;
    rdfs:label "Towards AI that understands the Real World." ;
    nk:about nk:topic-agents,
        nk:topic-multimodal,
        nk:topic-reasoning-math ;
    nk:inSession nk:session-25-930-session-1-keynote-1-pasc ;
    nk:summary "Recent advances in AI have been driven by large-scale generative models with impressive capabilities in language, code, and digital tasks. Yet these systems still have a limited understanding of the physical world, human intentions, and real-world context." ;
    nk:talkType "Keynote" ;
    nk:time "2026-10-25 09:30–10:30" ;
    nk:url "https://2026.emnlp.org/program/keynotes/" .

nk:talk-keynote-2-graham-neubig a nk:Talk ;
    rdfs:label "On the Value of Open Research in Language Modeling - An Adversarial Dialog" ;
    nk:about nk:topic-llms,
        nk:topic-open-research ;
    nk:inSession nk:session-26-1515-session-8-keynote-2-grah ;
    nk:summary "Large language models are simultaneously one of the greatest advances in natural language processing ever and one of the most confounding for the open research community. Given the extreme resource intensiveness and economic value of research in this area, much research has moved out of the public e" ;
    nk:talkType "Keynote" ;
    nk:time "2026-10-26 15:15–16:15" ;
    nk:url "https://2026.emnlp.org/program/keynotes/" .

nk:talk-keynote-3-anna-korhonen a nk:Talk ;
    rdfs:label "AI for the Many: Starting from the World, Not the Model" ;
    nk:about nk:topic-multilingual-nlp ;
    nk:inSession nk:session-27-1400-session-12-keynote-3-ann ;
    nk:summary "AI is advancing at extraordinary speed, but its benefits remain profoundly uneven. For much of the world, the dominant path towards ever larger, more resource-intensive models is out of reach and not necessarily the right one." ;
    nk:talkType "Keynote" ;
    nk:time "2026-10-27 14:00–15:00" ;
    nk:url "https://2026.emnlp.org/program/keynotes/" .

