    nk:summary "MINT: Multimodal Interaction in Face-to-Face Dialogue is a one-day workshop that targets a core limitation in current “multimodal NLP”: most approaches treat nonverbal signals (gesture, facial expression, gaze, body pose, prosody) as auxiliary context to language, or as post-hoc outputs generated af" ;
